{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888571,"nonce":"OnYSIIkJHJ9v3iyyyGkis0Y80ig=","title":"There is no setup guide for VictoriaMetrics, so an operator cannot tell that vmalert must go through Alertmanager and be paired as the rule source","message":"**What is wrong.** `docs/setup/` has `configuration.md`, `slack.md`, `tuning.md`, `slack-live-verification.md`; none mentions vmalert.\n\n**Where.** New `docs/setup/victoriametrics.md` (+ docs-site mirror): vmalert `-notifier.url` → Alertmanager → oto webhook (no direct vmalert ingest — the reconciler, ADR 0006, reads suppressed state from Alertmanager's `/api/v2/alerts`); set the source's Prometheus URL to vmalert; recommend `-external.alert.source='vmui/#/?g0.expr={{.Expr|queryEscape}}'` so the primary strategy works; note `-external.label` and that VictoriaLogs (`vlogs`) rules carry LogsQL, which rule snapshots store verbatim (expr diff is lexical, `internal/rules/domain/exprdiff.go`).\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** The guide exists, every flag in it was checked against the vmalert docs, and it links from `configuration.md`.\n\n**Blocked by.** `766709c`, `5a79ff5`, `d8fedb8`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}